abstract: >-
Structural Recognition above Metric Similarity (SRMS) presents a
recognition-centered computational architecture for future AI. The
repository argues that structural identity, critical deltas, decision
boundaries, runtime activation, Runtime Invariants, structural confidence,
and certified structural assets should be established before metric
similarity performs ranking and optimization. It introduces the Base-Delta
Asymmetry Principle, Recognition-Gated Cosine Scoring, Small but Decisive
Structural Deltas, Structural Recognition as Runtime Intelligence,
Structural Confidence Accumulation, Certified Structural Components, and
the Structural Recognition Pipeline for Future AI. Its central principle is
that recognition establishes the computational world, while similarity
optimizes inside that world.

